  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Georgia received $8.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Award activity in Georgia reached 78,378 awards, with an average award size of $114K. Obligations fell 23.6% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $4.7B, making the Department of Defense the largest buyer in the state for the current fiscal year to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $1.4B and the General Services Administration obligated $1B, placing those agencies among the top buyers. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP received $710M, making LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP the largest single vendor by obligations. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction led industries with $1.1B, and Aircraft Manufacturing followed with $807M. Historical standings show variability: FY21 and FY23 each recorded $11.1B, FY22 recorded $8.5B, FY24 recorded $10.4B, and FY25 recorded $11.6B. The figures are contract obligations and the current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have federal obligations to Georgia changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year totals show variation: FY21 recorded $11.1B, FY22 recorded $8.5B, FY23 recorded $11.1B, FY24 recorded $10.4B, FY25 recorded $11.6B, and FY26 recorded $8.9B. Obligations fell 23.6% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date period. The Department of Defense obligated $4.7B in FY2026 to date, a large share of the current-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate Georgia contract spending right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense, the Department of Health and Human Services, and the General Services Administration are the top three buyers, with $4.7B, $1.4B, and $1B respectively. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP, MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE, and GEORGIA TECH APPLIED RESEARCH CORP are the top three vendors, with $710M, $492M, and $299M respectively. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Aircraft Manufacturing are the top two industries, with $1.1B and $807M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
